{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109974","id":2773333094,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6lTbRm","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109974","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109974.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109974.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109974","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109974/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109974/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109974/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/038f5934e70491235106e28911621ebedd57fb3f","number":109974,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"SwiftUI lifecycle for Apple embedded platforms","user":{"login":"rsanchezsaez","id":444313,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0NDMxMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/444313?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsanchezsaez","html_url":"https://github.com/rsanchezsaez","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsanchezsaez/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsanchezsaez/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsanchezsaez/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsanchezsaez/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsanchezsaez/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsanchezsaez/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsanchezsaez/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsanchezsaez/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsanchezsaez/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Dear Godot community,\r\n\r\nThis PR is a followup to https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105628 (I encourage you to read the description of that PR, where I outlined the plan, to get the full context for this contribution).\r\n\r\nThis change adds Swift compilation support to SCons, and adopts the SwiftUI lifecycle on Apple embedded platforms, which is the modern way of instantiating apps on Apple platforms. This is a pre-requesite for launching an immersive scene on visionOS.\r\n\r\nThis PR builds on top of https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107789, so that one should be merged first.\r\n\r\ncc @BastiaanOlij @stuartcarnie @bruvzg  \r\n\r\n## Technical Discussion\r\n\r\nI have developed and tested these changes using [Xcode 26 beta 6 (17A5305f)](https://developer.apple.com/download/applications).\r\n\r\n### Minimum Deployment Targets\r\n\r\nThis PR increases the minimum deployment targets to iOS 14.0 (which is the minimum supported version for SwiftUI app lifecycle), and visionOS 26.0. We believe increasing the iOS target to 14.0 is acceptable given the age of that release.\r\n \r\n### SCons\r\n\r\nThere are parts of SCons I don't understand very well, and the current approach for compiling Swift is based on trial and error. I think the way the Builder is implemented a bit unorthodox, because Swift projects don't have header files, so you must pass all Swift files to the compiler.\r\n\r\nI have tested that if there are more than one Swift file in the same subfolder, the are compiled and linked successfully.\r\n\r\nIf any SCons experts have suggestions for improving this aspect, we'd be happy to iterate on the solution.\r\n\r\n## Testing\r\n\r\nWe have been testing this PR with the [Platformer demo project](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-demo-projects/tree/master/3d/platformer). We have verified the project continues to work on iOS and visionOS, both with the Mobile and Forward+ renderers using the Metal rendering driver.\r\n\r\n## Missing Functionality\r\n\r\n- The DPI metrics on visionOS are still hardcoded for now. They can change at runtime depending on how close the window is to the viewer. I think this is not a big deal breaker at this point of time. We may address this functionality in a separate PR in the future.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097519,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc1MTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/platform:ios","name":"platform:ios","description":"","color":"e4e4e4","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098009,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgwMDk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:buildsystem","name":"topic:buildsystem","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":12939969,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AxXLB","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/23","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/23","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/23/labels","number":23,"state":"closed","title":"4.6","description":"","creator":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://a